## 4. ID Prefix Registry

### 4.1 Specification Prefixes (Layer 1)

| Prefix | Usage | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| REQ- | Requirement | [REQ-AUTH-EXPIRY], [REQ-IDEMPOTENT-WRITE] |
| SYS- | System / subsystem definition | [SYS-INGEST], [SYS-SCHEDULER] |
| CMP- | Component responsibility | [CMP-ROUTER], [CMP-STORE] |
| API- | External interface contract | [API-CREATE-ORDER], [API-V2-SEARCH] |
| IF- | Internal interface / contract | [IF-QUEUE-CONSUMER] |
| SCHEMA- | Data model / schema node | [SCHEMA-ORDER], [SCHEMA-EVENT-ENVELOPE] |
| INV- | Invariant / constraint | [INV-NO-ORPHAN-CHILD], [INV-MONOTONIC-CLOCK] |
| NFR- | Non-functional requirement | [NFR-P99-LATENCY], [NFR-RPO] |
| CFG- | Configuration surface | [CFG-RETRY-POLICY], [CFG-FEATURE-FLAGS] |

### 4.2 Implementation Prefixes (Layer 2)

| Prefix | Usage | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| MOD- | Module / package | [MOD-PARSER], [MOD-HTTP-CLIENT] |
| SVC- | Deployable service | [SVC-API-GATEWAY], [SVC-WORKER] |
| FN- | Public function / method surface | [FN-VALIDATE-TOKEN] |
| EP- | Realized endpoint / handler | [EP-POST-ORDERS] |
| DEP- | Runtime / build dependency | [DEP-DATASTORE], [DEP-MESSAGE-BUS] |
| DEV- | Deviation from specification | [DEV-RETRY-UNBOUNDED], [DEV-SCHEMA-EXTRA-FIELD] |

### 4.3 Verification Prefixes (Layer 3)

| Prefix | Usage | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| TEST- | Test suite / case | [TEST-AUTH-EXPIRY], [TEST-IDEMPOTENCY] |
| CHK- | Static / property / lint check | [CHK-NO-CYCLES], [CHK-SCHEMA-BACKCOMPAT] |
| AC- | Acceptance criterion | [AC-CHECKOUT-HAPPY-PATH] |
| GATE- | Release / merge gate | [GATE-COVERAGE], [GATE-DRC] |

### 4.4 Decision Prefixes (Layer 4)

| Prefix | Usage | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| DEC- | Engineering / architectural decision | [DEC-EVENT-SOURCING], [DEC-MONOREPO] |
| TRD- | Recorded trade-off analysis | [TRD-SYNC-VS-ASYNC] |
| RISK- | Engineering risk | [RISK-SINGLE-WRITER], [RISK-VENDOR-LOCKIN] |

